  "body": "Follow-up of #1749 (draft PR #1772). Found by the #1749 worker and filed by SKULL.\n\n**What happens.** PR #1772 grows an untilted whole-model 3D Pocket's footprint by the tool radius (less 0.01 mm) where a level is open to air. Two cases are still outside that change and can leave stock standing while the op reports `ok`:\n\n1. **A tilted (3+2) 3D Pocket** still uses the old footprint, the silhouette shrunk by the tool radius. An open-sided notch keeps a band one radius wide at full stock height, which is the #1749 ridge.\n2. **Stock reaching more than about two tool radii past the silhouette** is not cleared on an open side. The grown footprint stops at the silhouette edge plus about a radius.\n\n**What must happen.** Either the open side is cleared out to the stock outline, as the 2D pocket has done since #12, with no cutter position entering any part; or the op names the uncleared band in a warning, or is marked incomplete. It must never read `ok` over standing stock.\n\n**Done means**\n- A pinning test for each case, built in code like `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_open_side.rs`. It measures the carried stock along the open edge and requires either the floor or a named warning or incomplete.\n- A gouge check: no cutter position inside a part.\n- Each new line mutation-checked.\n\nPart of #1749's area. See `docs/decisions/1749-pocket3d-open-side.md` on PR #1772's branch.",
